From f8db4290fb54e943869b838165f448060dfa8d95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jgrizon
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:08:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: prototype sampleGrad for the AGX pixel-sample
 failure, key the cache

VICTORY_PS_SAMPLE_GRAD=1 emits a pixel program's implicit-LOD image_sample
(op 60, not a cube's and not with offsets past the existing path) as
sampleGrad (63), with the coarse derivative of each coordinate for both
directions: D3DMetal on AGX M1 fails some mesh/PS pipelines with
`air.sample_.v4f32`. Upstream's prototype uses the x derivative for both
directions; this uses dx and dy as lower's bias-as-gradients path does. Off
by default.

The shader cache key did not cover the diagnostic emitter switches, so
VICTORY_BARRIER_LDS=1 would have reused DXIL emitted with mode 1|2|8. Both
are now read once (victory_shader::emit::{barrier_lds, ps_sample_grad}) and
hashed into the key, adding nothing while off like the other options.

Ported from paveledits/ScarlettMac runtime-preview/checkpoint/patches/0010-shader-key-the-cache-on-VICTORY_BARRIER_LDS-and-prot.patch

Generated by Mistral Vibe.
Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>
